alysis the plan's new guard requires","Codebase: 18+ scripts/check_*.py guards use ast.parse (check_destructive_test_exec.py, check_wall_clock_asserts.py, check_tickets_boundary.py, ...), the repo's established banned-construct enforcement convention, wired into make lint (Makefile:278-299)","Makefile:272-278 records story bold-abeyant-indri moving a test-hygiene gate into a scripts/check_*.py reachable from BOTH CI and make lint so a local-green/CI-red split cannot happen — the exact concern the plan's Symptom opens with ('CI can never exercise this path')","Retrieved prior art confirms the point-fix half is sound (git 2.38.0 RelNotes; GitHub 2.38 blog: 'Git will only work with bare repositories specified by the top-level --git-dir argument'; git safe.adoc), so the prior-art gap is specific to the new guard mechanism, not the fix"],"finding":"The plan's step-2 guard reinvents the repo's established scripts/check_*.py AST-guard pattern without considering that prior art or reusing check_raw_git_writes.py's near-identical argv-and-helper-forwarding analysis; it embeds a bespoke tree-derived AST scan inside a pytest oracle and dismisses check_raw_git_writes.py as merely 'an unrelated concern' on the basis of subject matter rather than mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa64a720ac26d8267","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', step 2 (tree-derived static AST scan) and 'This is a recurrence of a class already fixed' (\"scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py covers an unrelated concern\")","norm_id":"nc50195d0449fe0d5","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future bare-fixture test reintroduces git -C <bare> in src/ or scripts/ rather than tests/, where the pytest-scoped oracle does not look but a lint guard would","The guard passes locally under pytest but the make lint / CI lint stage — where every other banned-construct guard lives — has no corresponding gate, re-creating a local/CI verdict split"